    "interpretation": "For the MR/d2 estimator the guaranteed (5th-pct) in-control ARL0 at the module pilot baseline (m=20-30) is even lower than for S/c4: the less efficient estimator makes an unlucky-baseline false-alarm rate MORE likely. The <=5% false-alarm budget still holds in EXPECTATION (median 30-batch false alarms << 1.5) but guaranteed near-nominal ARL0 needs a substantially larger baseline than for S/c4, reinforcing Quesenberry's m>=300 rule as a floor rather than a ceiling when MR/d2 is used.",
    "smallest_tabulated_m_meeting_target_MR": null
  },
  "closes": [
    "Quantifies, for the first time in this module, the estimated-parameter ARL0 degradation of the MONTGOMERY-DEFAULT moving-range (MRbar/d2) sigma estimator for the Shewhart Individuals chart -- the FIRST does_not_close item of estparam-arl-degradation-v1.",
    "Derives the exact closed-form MR sampling variance from the adjacent moving-range correlation (rho=-1/2, bivariate folded-normal cross moment) and VALIDATES it against direct pinned-seed correlated Monte Carlo (rel err < 3%, estimator confirmed unbiased).",
    "Computes the Patnaik effective df nu_eff(m) < (m-1) and the ~0.61 asymptotic relative efficiency of MR/d2 vs S/c4, corroborating Cryer & Ryan 1990.",
    "Shows the MR/d2 guaranteed (5th-pct) in-control ARL0 sits BELOW the S/c4 value at every finite baseline m, turning 'degrades at least as much (conservative direction)' into signed numbers and recovering the known-parameter 370.398 as the m->inf limit."
  ],
  "detector_design": {
    "convention_note": "Both estimators use limits = mu_hat +/- L*sigma_hat with the SAME L=3, so the only difference is estimator sampling variance (apples-to-apples efficiency comparison). This uses the UNBIASED S/c4; estparam-arl-degradation-v1 used the biased limits=Xbar+/-L*S convention, so its S-numbers are not directly comparable to the S/c4 reference tabulated here.",
    "limits_sigma": 3.0,
    "mu_estimator": "Xbar",
    "primary_sigma_estimator": "MRbar/d2 (moving range span 2, UNBIASED)",
    "reference_sigma_estimator": "S/c4 (UNBIASED)",
    "type": "Shewhart Individuals"
  },
  "does_not_close": [
    "Does NOT establish real-batch acceptability, product qualification, EHS acceptability, or batch-release authority.",
    "Assumes i.i.d. normal in-control data; non-normality and autocorrelation (which bias MRbar and break the rho=-1/2 structure) are not modeled and remain open.",
    "Estimated-parameter EWMA (Jones, Champ, Rigdon 2001) and CUSUM guaranteed-ARL under estimated parameters remain open Phase-1 gaps.",
    "Covers the span-2 moving range (d2(2)); larger MR spans and the median-MR estimator are not characterized.",
    "No prospective time-ordered 30-batch pilot is checked in; this is a theory characterization, not a recall/false-alarm measurement on real batches."
  ],
