  "headline": "Moving-range (MRbar/d2) estimated-parameter ARL0 degradation for the module's Shewhart Individuals chart (L=3). The Individuals-chart textbook-default sigma estimator is the average moving range, sigma_hat=MRbar/d2, NOT the sample S used by the prior receipt. An exact closed-form MR sampling variance (adjacent moving-range correlation rho=-1/2) -- validated against pinned-seed correlated Monte Carlo -- yields a Patnaik effective df nu_eff(m) BELOW the S/c4 df (m-1), and the estimated-parameter guaranteed (5th-pct) in-control ARL0 for MR/d2 sits BELOW the S/c4 value at every finite baseline m. This quantifies the 'MR/d2 degrades at least as much (conservative direction)' assertion that estparam-arl-degradation-v1 left unquantified.",
